The change modifies the `Mcpx` builder, so that, optionally, users may provide a profile:

```java
        // Instantiate a new Mcpx client with the configuration values.
        var mcpx = Mcpx.forApiKey(apiKey)
            .withBaseUrl(baseUrl)
            .withProfile(profileId)
            .build();
        // Refresh the installed servlets definitions from mcp.run.
        // This will load the configuration once.
        // You can schedule this invocation periodically to refresh
        // such configuration.
        mcpx.refreshInstallations();
```

This makes the `mcpx` object effectively scoped to a single profile: this is intended to make cache management simpler.

This PR implements [Project 1](https://cs50.harvard.edu/games/2018/projects/1/flappy/). The requirements were:
- Influence the generation of pipes so as to bring about more complicated level generation;
- Give the player a medal for their performance, along with their score;
- Implement a pause feature, just in case life gets in the way of jumping through pipes.

I've also added dev container files and a README.

Changes applied by PR

Implements NinjaMapper to convert NinjaModel into NinjaDTO;
Creation of DTO including all necessary fields to extern communication;
Refactors NinjaService to use DTO, excluding the model exposition;
Adjust the NinjaController to include DTO; 

These changes bring to this code a better organization and separation of responsibilities, making it easier to maintenance and future improvements, besides providing more security to database.

